# Patch files are applied with `git apply`, which matches context bytes literally.
# Any end-of-line conversion on checkout corrupts them: with core.autocrlf=true a
# 268,931-byte patch is checked out as 274,366 bytes and no longer applies. Mark
# every patch as non-text so the working copy is always byte-identical to the blob,
# independent of the machine's autocrlf setting.
*.patch -text
third_party/patches/*.patch whitespace=-blank-at-eol
